The linker errors indicate that several `regulator_fake_..._reset` functions and `regulator_fake_..._fake` structures are undefined. These symbols are part of the Fake Function Framework (FFF) and are generated when `DEFINE_FFF_GLOBALS;` is processed, provided that the corresponding fake functions have been declared using `FAKE_VALUE_FUNC` or `FAKE_VOID_FUNC`.

The `tests/drivers/regulator/api/src/main.c` file includes `<zephyr/drivers/regulator/fake.h>` and calls `DEFINE_FFF_GLOBALS;`. The `regulator_fake_...` functions are expected to be declared in `zephyr/drivers/regulator/fake.h`.

The `drivers/regulator/Kconfig.fake` file shows that the `REGULATOR_FAKE` Kconfig option, which enables the FFF-based fake regulator driver, depends on `DT_HAS_ZEPHYR_FAKE_REGULATER_ENABLED`. This Kconfig option is crucial because the `zephyr/drivers/regulator/fake.h` header (or the C file implementing the fake driver) likely wraps its FFF declarations and definitions within an `#ifdef CONFIG_REGULATOR_FAKE` block.

The `tests/drivers/regulator/api/app.overlay` currently defines a `regulator` node without a `compatible` property:
```dts
/ {
	regulator: regulator {
		reg0: REG0 {};
		// ...
	};
};
```
Without a `compatible = "zephyr,fake-regulator";` property on the `regulator` node, the `DT_HAS_ZEPHYR_FAKE_REGULATER_ENABLED` Kconfig symbol will not be set, and consequently, `CONFIG_REGULATOR_FAKE` will not be enabled. This prevents the FFF declarations and definitions from being included in the build, leading to the "undefined reference" linker errors for the fake functions and their reset counterparts.

Additionally, the linker errors like `undefined reference to `__device_dts_ord_40'` and `__device_dts_ord_43'` are related to device tree nodes (`reg0` and `reg3`). These errors occur when `DEVICE_DT_GET` is used for a device that doesn't have an associated driver instantiated by the build system. By adding the `compatible` property, the fake regulator driver will be enabled and correctly bind to these device tree nodes, resolving these errors as well.

The fix is to add the `compatible = "zephyr,fake-regulator";` property to the `regulator` node in `tests/drivers/regulator/api/app.overlay`.

